From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: pkgdemon <jpm820@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 07:00:00 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] NextBSD: loader graphical boot on virtio-gpu VMs

On a VM whose display is virtio-gpu (UTM; QEMU -vga none), boot-video
graphics mode (0011) never started (nextbsd/nextbsd-freebsd-compat#91):

- OVMF connects only the devices its boot needs, so virtio-gpu-pci was
  never started and there was no GOP at all.  When nothing produced a
  GOP, the loader now connects the PCI display controllers (base class
  0x03), and VirtioGpuDxe brings one up.  That display's GOP goes first
  in ConOut, once, so the firmware lights it on later boots instead of
  leaving it inactive until the loader runs.
- virtio-gpu's GOP is blit-only under OVMF and AAVMF alike, which
  efi_find_framebuffer() skipped, leaving the firmware's text console
  and its cursor.  A blit-only GOP is now used when no GOP has a linear
  framebuffer: gfx_fb draws through gop->Blt() while boot services run,
  and the boot_video record carries no address, so the kernel's
  virtio_gpu(4) takes the display over from the splash
  (nextbsd/nextbsd-kernel#437).
- Any serial port in ConOut meant text.  Only a serial-primary ConOut
  (RB_SERIAL) does now.  A serial port behind the screen (RB_MULTIPLE
  alone: QEMU, UTM, a BMC redirect) is mirrored instead: the loader's
  text goes to that port's own terminal as well as the replay ring, the
  autoboot countdown runs, and a key typed on that port reaches the
  prompt and leaves graphics mode, while the keyboard is still ignored.
  CI keeps typing its console contract over serial.  RB_MULTIPLE that
  came only from ConOut is not exported, so the kernel's splash stays.

Carried out-of-tree for NextBSD.
